Key Takeaways:
LLMs are trained to predict the next token. Do it at massive scale and understanding, reasoning, and code generation emerge as side effects.
Tokens are the billing and memory unit. ~¾ word per token. Context window = working memory. Long log files won't fit in one call → chunking is a real engineering problem for capstone.
Prompt engineering is the main control lever. Four techniques: system prompt (set the role), few-shot (show examples), chain of thought (reason step by step), RAG (inject retrieved context). Key is to prompt well.
Three new risks with generative AI: hallucination (confidently wrong), prompt injection (log line hijacks your system prompt), content filtering (Azure has it built in).
Ollama = free local LLMs. No API key, no cost, runs on laptop.
One-liner: LLMs predict tokens, but at scale that becomes reasoning — and we control the output through prompts, not code.
